From: Arctic Linux maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Do not advertise DMA-BUF without a renderer DRM device

Scenefx's software EGL renderer can expose texture import formats without a
DRM descriptor. wlroots cannot create DRM/DMA-BUF globals in that case, and
passing its NULL DMA-BUF result to the scene crashes compositor startup.
Keep wl_shm available and create device-dependent globals only with a DRM FD.
The accelerated renderer path and hardware buffer support remain intact.

--- a/src/main.c
+++ b/src/main.c
@@ -494,8 +494,9 @@
 	 * integrate it with wlr_scene. */
 	wlr_renderer_init_wl_shm(server.renderer, server.display);
 
-	if (wlr_renderer_get_texture_formats(server.renderer,
-										 WLR_BUFFER_CAP_DMABUF)) {
+	drm_fd = wlr_renderer_get_drm_fd(server.renderer);
+	if (drm_fd >= 0 && wlr_renderer_get_texture_formats(server.renderer,
+																 WLR_BUFFER_CAP_DMABUF)) {
 		wlr_drm_create(server.display, server.renderer);
 		wlr_scene_set_linux_dmabuf_v1(server.scene,
 									  wlr_linux_dmabuf_v1_create_with_renderer(
